<title>CHINA: HK May orders on hand fall eight pct yr on yr.</title>
<headline>HK May orders on hand fall eight pct yr on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Census and Statistics Department said May orders-on-hand fell eight percent in value on the year against a 10 percent drop in April.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value of orders-on-hand in May 1997 over May 1996 (* means that comparative figure has been revised and *** means that the change is within +/- 0.5 percent):</p>
<p>						  May 1997   April 1997</p>
<p> All industries covered in the survey  -8	    -10</p>
<p> Wearing apparel			     -7	     -5*</p>
<p> Textiles					-5	     -8</p>
<p>						  May 1997   April 1997</p>
<p> Electronic Products			-12	    -16</p>
<p> Electrical products			 -9	     -3</p>
<p> Fabricated metal products		-10	    -17*</p>
<p> Plastic products			   -19	    -17</p>
<p> Printing and publishing		  +10	    +11*</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
